Port the core HTTP parser interface from Java to an Ecstasy `.x` file. Target: `lib_relaxf` module.

The Java source (Colin's production, commit 99544ab) is `Rfc822HeaderState` — a state machine that:
1. Accumulates bytes from a ByteBuffer into a header buffer
2. Scans for `\r\n\r\n` (HTTP header terminator)
3. Parses the request line (method, path, protocol) or response status
4. Extracts named headers

The Ecstasy equivalent should be a `service` that wraps a JNP-backed `MemSeg` (zero-copy off-heap memory) for buffer management.

Context: the XVM project already has these libs:
- `javatools_jitbridge/.../nMemSeg.java` — wraps java.lang.foreign.MemorySegment + Arena
- `lib_relaxf/src/main/x/one/xio/MemSeg.x` — service MemSeg(Int size)
- `lib_relaxf/src/main/x/one/xio/Callback.x` — const Callback

Write: **lib_relaxf/src/main/x/relaxf/http/HttpParser.x**

The Ecstasy service:
```ecstasy
/**
 * HTTP/1.1 request/response parser. Ported from Rfc822HeaderState.
 * Uses MemSeg for zero-copy buffer management.
 */
service HttpParser(MemSeg buffer) {
    @RO Boolean complete;
    @RO String method;
    @RO String path;
    @RO String protocol;

    void reset();
    Boolean read(Int fd);
    String header(String name);
}
```

Methods:
- `reset()` — clears the state machine for a new request
- `read(Int fd)` — reads bytes from the fd into the buffer, scans for terminator, returns True when headers complete
- `header(String name)` — returns the value of a named header (case-insensitive)
- `complete` property — True when `\r\n\r\n` has been found
- `method`, `path`, `protocol` — extracted from the request line

